; ====================================================================
; strings.cases
; Conformance corpus for the Pasta / Basta STRING grammar.
;
; Strings are raw -- there are no escape sequences anywhere in the format.
; The multiline form is the escape hatch, and it is a raw one: its body ends
; at the first run of three or more quotes, and where that run is longer than
; three, only the final three close the string and the extras belong to the
; content.  See ../Basta.txt (STRINGS ARE RAW / MULTILINE DELIMITER RULE).
;
; FORMAT / FINGERPRINT are identical to atom-labels.cases; see that file.
; In <input>, \n means a newline and \ a literal backslash.
; ====================================================================

; --- simple form ------------------------------------------------------
> {d: "plain"}
= {d=str:plain}
> {d: ""}
= {d=str:}
> {d: "C:\path\to\file"}
= {d=str:C:\path\to\file}

; --- a quote needs the multiline form ---------------------------------
> {d: """a " b"""}
= {d=str:a " b}
> {d: """said "hi" today"""}
= {d=str:said "hi" today}
> {d: """"leading"""}
= {d=str:"leading}

; --- quote-run rule: extras in the closing run are content ------------
> {d: """a"""}
= {d=str:a}
> {d: """ends q""""}
= {d=str:ends q"}
> {d: """two"""""}
= {d=str:two""}
> {d: """"""""}
= {d=str:""}
> {d: """a "" b"""}
= {d=str:a "" b}

; --- newlines ---------------------------------------------------------
> {d: """line one\nline two"""}
= {d=str:line one\nline two}

; --- malformed --------------------------------------------------------
> {d: "unterminated}
= ERR
> {d: """unterminated}
= ERR
